set_option linter.unusedVariables false

/-!
# A331117

Lexicographically earliest sequence of distinct terms such that a(n+1) = a(n) + the largest odd digit of a(n), starting with a(n) = 1. If this addition is impossible, or if it leads to a term already in the sequence, restart the sequence from there with the smallest unused integer.

The 81 terms known to OEIS, indexed from `1`.

Skeleton generated by `lake exe oeis-gen`; every declaration is a `sorry` placeholder.
-/

namespace A331117

/-- Known terms of `A331117`, starting at index `1`. -/
def data : List retType :=
  [1, 2, 3, 6, 4, 5, 10, 11, 12, 13,
    16, 17, 24, 7, 14, 15, 20, 8, 9, 18,
    19, 28, 21, 22, 23, 26, 25, 30, 33, 36,
